 the trajectory of the club and the bending of the shaft will change the timing of impact and the direction of the face, leading to missed shots.\n\n-What is rhythm tempo?\nRhythm = time signature (2, 3, 4 time signature, etc.)\n\nRegarding the rhythm, there is no correct answer, but if it is in triple time.\n\n1 is the address (forward press)\n2 is from backswing to top\n3 impacts from downswing\n\nTempo = speed (count number per minute)\nIf the speed is 60 counts per minute (1 count per second), it will be \"60 BPM\".\nBPM (Beats Per Minute)\n\n-Recommended usage (in the case of 3 beats)\n[1]Normal recording\n\n[2]Tap the metronome icon during playback (nice shot)\nWhile advancing frame by frame in the paused state\n(1)Tap start (green) when starting the ing\n(2)Tap top (yellow) by turning the top\n(3)Tap finish (red) at the finish\n\n[3]Two tempo values ​​are displayed\n(Same BPM if the rhythm is the same)\n\n[4]If you know the tempo, start the metronome (set the value of [3]) and swing recording according to that tempo.\n\n[5]Swing check\n\n[6]Practice so that you can always swing at the same tempo\n(In general, the ideal tempo is the same for all drivers, irons, and butters.)\n\n\n~Main functions~\n\n1.Swing tempo measurement with metronome\n\n2.Slow playback by jog shuttle\n*When rotating, it vibrates in units of one frame, so you can feel the slow motion.\n\n*1 will be available after billing.\n\n\n3.Independent lock function (with camera zoom function)\n・ Focus lock (AF)\n・ Exposure lock (AE)\n\n4.Line drawing\nYou can freely manipulate the swing plane, shaft plane, and the circle at the head position!\n\n- The line can be rotated 360 degrees (two fingers)\n- The length of the line can be adjusted freely (two fingers)\n- Lines and circles can be moved\n(The size of the circle can be changed with two fingers)\n\n5.Recording start self-timer\nIt is possible to sound the alarm from 3 seconds before the start of recording\n*A large countdown is displayed even when the alarm is off.\n\n6.Video comparison (1 & 2 screen)\nIn the one-screen overlap mode, you can freely change the position of the superimposed video and the size of the image, so it is possible to match the size of two people exactly.\n*If you lay the iPhone sideways, it will switch to 2 screens.\n\n7.Swing image output (25 consecutive photos)\nFreely set the output start position and end position with the playback slider\n* You can convert the video to JPG → edit it.\n\n8.Folder function\nBy dividing into folders according to the type of club, etc.\nYou can quickly find the swing video you want to watch.\n\n*Professional swing recording\nYou can download multiple professional videos.\n\nIn collaboration with JOYX Co., Ltd.\nProfessional golfer Richard Tate\nCooperated with the shooting.\n\n-Richard Tate\n(Affiliation: Chubu Co., Ltd.)\nhttps://www.danketurf.com\n\nBorn June 20, 1972\nHeight 178 cm, weight 78 kg.\nHis father is Australian and his mother is Japanese.\nHe was born in Hong Kong, grew up in Yokohama from 4 to 10 years old, and then went to Australia.", "languageCodesISO2A": ["EN", "JA"], "fileSizeBytes": "38692864", "formattedPrice": "￦1,100", "userRatingCountForCurrentVersion": 2, "trackContentRating": "4+", "averageUserRatingForCurrentVersion": 5, "sellerUrl": "https://ik-software-app.com", "releaseNotes": "Added a 'Share' button to Backup/Restore. \nFixed a bug that caused the app to crash when cutting a video extremely short during video editing.", "trackId": 396029913, "trackName": "Golf Swing Check - Slow Movie", "bundleId": "jp.IKsoftware.BestSwing", "userRatingCount": 2}]}